<table border="0" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" width="100%"><tr><td>
<a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=20"><img src="images/topics/live.gif" border="0" Alt="Live" align="right" hspace="10" vspace="10"></a>
<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000"><P>This is what we&nbsp;published on May 29 (source: <STRONG>Townhall.com</STRONG>):</P><STRONG>Madonna</STRONG>, who has launched her racy new <STRONG>"Reinvention World Tour,"</STRONG> is the featured <STRONG>attraction of a fund-raiser by one of the "527" Democratic fund-raising committees designed to get around the McCain-Feingold Act's ban on soft money.</STRONG> 
<P><STRONG>Two tickets cost $5,000 for "an evening with Madonna" June 14 at the MCI Center in downtown Washington</STRONG>. It is sponsored by the Great Plains Leadership Fund, supposedly "independent" but actually a Democratic fund-raising organization.</P>
<P>The fund's "honorary chair" is Democratic Sen. Byron L. Dorgan of North Dakota, an advocate of the McCain-Feingold bill. Its headquarters is nowhere near the Great Plains, but is located on Capitol Hill in Washington.</P>
<P><STRONG>KSJB-AM.com</STRONG> gave more details:</P>
<P>Tickets for a concert that features war and sex await donors to <STRONG>Senator Byron Dorgan</STRONG>. <STRONG>CNN reports $5000 donors to his Great Plains Leadership Fund will get two tickets on Monday for Madonna's June 14 concert at the MCI center in Washington, D.C.</STRONG> The singer's current concert features images of war and bisexual themes including simulated sex acts between <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> and members of her dance troupe. U.S. Senate candidate <STRONG>Mike Liffrig</STRONG> said in a news release if the Great Plains Leadership PAC "was really interested in promoting the <STRONG>Great Plains</STRONG>, <STRONG>Dorgan</STRONG> should reward donors with tickets to the new <STRONG>Bully Pulpit</STRONG> golf course in <STRONG>Medora</STRONG>, a <STRONG>Trollwood Park Theatre</STRONG> production in <STRONG>Fargo</STRONG> or something that encourages his powerful donors to experience our state's many hidden treasures." </P>
</font></div>
</td></tr></table>


</td></tr></table>


