<table border="0" cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFA8D3" width="100%"><tr><td align="left">
<font class="storytitle" color="#FFFFFF"><b><a href="modules.php?name=News&amp;file=categories&amp;op=newindex&amp;catid=3"><font class="storycat">Rumours</font></a>: Madonna and Britney to repeat snog?</b></font>
</td></tr></table></td></tr></table>

<table border="0" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" width="100%"><tr><td>
<a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=20"><img src="images/topics/live.gif" border="0" Alt="Live" align="right" hspace="10" vspace="10"></a>
<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000"><P><SPAN class=norm12><FONT face=Verdana><STRONG>Sun'Bizarre column:</STRONG></FONT></SPAN></P>
<P><SPAN class=norm12><FONT face=Verdana><STRONG>MADONNA</STRONG> and <STRONG>BRITNEY</STRONG> <STRONG>SPEARS</STRONG> want to recreate their infamous on-stage snog.<BR><BR><STRONG>Madge has asked Britney to sing with her on Wednesday at the first of six New York shows of her world tour — and insiders say the pair are on for a replay of their kiss.<BR></STRONG><BR>The original came in August when they stunned a celebrity audience at the <STRONG>MTV Video Music Awards</STRONG> by suddenly locking lips during a duet of Madonna’s song Hollywood.<BR><BR>The pair loved the fuss it caused and have been eagerly discussing a repeat performance for the last month.<BR></FONT><EM><BR><FONT face=Verdana>But their plans suffered a setback last week when Britney hurt her knee falling during a video shoot in the Big Apple.<BR></FONT></EM><BR><FONT face=Verdana><STRONG>Britney has promised Madge she’ll do her best to be fighting fit for Wednesday’s gig.<BR></STRONG><BR>A source told me: “Britney was delighted when Madonna asked her if she could join her on stage. They got loads of reaction the first time they kissed. She agreed to do it immediately. Their people have been faxing and e-mailing non-stop to sort things out. Everything was confirmed last week.<BR><BR>“Britney was gutted when she had her fall. It was pretty serious. She had to have surgery and she will find out this week how long she’ll be out of action.<BR><BR>“But she’s promised to do her best to be there on the night at Madison Square Garden. She just won’t be able to do strenuous dancing.”<BR><BR>If doctors ban Britney from performing she has until September — when Madonna’s Re-Invention tour finishes — to sort out another date.<BR></FONT><EM><BR><FONT face=Verdana><STRONG>Madonna has had her own health worries.</STRONG></FONT></EM><BR><BR><FONT face=Verdana>Last week I revealed she had been struck down for the second time with exhaustion just two weeks into her gruelling tour.<BR><BR>But now she is raring to go again.</FONT></SPAN></P>
</font></div>
</td></tr></table>


</td></tr></table>


<table border="0" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFA8D3" width="100%"><tr><td>
<table border="0" cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFDFEF" width="100%"><tr><td align="center">

<font class="content">Written by <a href="">gugarko</a> on Monday, June 14 @  W. Europe Daylight Time  [1 reads].</font><br>
<font class="content"">(<a href="modules.php?name=News&amp;file=article&amp;sid=3085">comments?</a> | <a href="modules.php?name=News&amp;file=categories&amp;op=newindex&amp;catid=3">Rumours</a> | Score: 0)</font>

</td></tr></table></td></tr></table>
<br><br><br><table border="0" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFA8D3" width="100%"><tr><td>
<table border="0" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFA8D3" width="100%"><tr><td>
<table border="0" cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFA8D3" width="100%"><tr><td align="left">
<font class="storytitle" color="#FFFFFF"><b>A Night with Madonna in DC.</b></font>
</td></tr></table></td></tr></table>

<table border="0" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" width="100%"><tr><td>
<a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=20"><img src="images/topics/live.gif" border="0" Alt="Live" align="right" hspace="10" vspace="10"></a>
<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000"><P>So it's <STRONG>June 13th</STRONG>, and we began the evening by standing in the long lines to enter into the <STRONG>MCI Center</STRONG> in <STRONG>Washington</STRONG>, <STRONG>DC</STRONG>. After about a half-hour, we were let in and I raced to the "program" stand and "shelled out 30 bucks for a beautiful tour book with images of Hebrew letters, beautiful <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG>'s, and a picture of which I have never seen before. It seems to be <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> when she was a little girl in a type of wedding dress. When we were allowed down into the arena, we took our seats at about 7:30 and I flipped through my tour book.<BR><BR><STRONG>We were in section 3, row W, seats 3 and 4.</STRONG> Of course, <STRONG>Madonna was late</STRONG>, like she was when she came for the <STRONG>2001 Drowned World Tour</STRONG> at the <STRONG>MCI Center</STRONG>. <STRONG>Two years ago, she was 2 hours late, but tonight, she was only about 30-40 minutes late. The arena was completely full.</STRONG> At around <STRONG>8:40</STRONG>, the lights went down, and two gigantic screens, put together, showed beautiful images of <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG>'s tour book and the <STRONG>Steven Klein</STRONG> spread. That's when the music began.<BR><BR>While watching the images, people were going crazy, but also listening to the <STRONG>"Beast Within"</STRONG> song. The screens open and there is <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> on a platform doing various Yoga poses and demanding us to <STRONG>"Vogue."</STRONG> At this point, I heard a lot of "Oh my god's" from various audience members (including myself). I'm sure you have read the various other reviews, so I will not comment on every single song she did because that would be monotonous.<BR><BR><STRONG>The audience tonight was excellent.</STRONG> I have never seen so many people dancing, clapping, and moving around at a concert. The majority of the people stood for the two-hour long show. There were so many images, so many sounds; it felt as if <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> was singing right there only to you. <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> was definitely right when she said that this show is an "assault on the senses." The highlights of the show included <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> on the catwalk for <STRONG>"American Life"</STRONG>. I was lucky enough to be right in front of her as she looked and "rapped" about drinking soy lattés, and having bodyguards and nannies. <BR><BR><STRONG>About halfway through the show, Madonna exclaimed that we were the best audience that she has had so far.</STRONG> After that comment, everyone just went crazy, again! I think generally, or at least from the comments I've heard from the fans at the concert and the people on the metro (who were leaving from the concert), most people seemed to be so proud and in "awe" that a 45 year old WOMAN can put on a show like that. As I was listening in to the girl on her cell phone, she said to the other person, "It was just incredible."<BR><BR>I think it was pretty incredible too.<BR><BR><STRONG>-Sean aka MrSpanishTeacher</STRONG></P>
<P><STRONG><EM>Keep on sending your reviews, pics, scans and whatever!</EM></STRONG></P>
</font></div>
</td></tr></table>


</td></tr></table>


